-- ======================
-- PART B: SELECT FOR UPDATE to lock a student record
-- Must be done using TWO separate sessions/clients connected to the DB.
-- Instructions below show exactly what to run in Session A and Session B.
-- ======================

-- Session A (in a client window):
-- 1) START TRANSACTION;
-- 2) SELECT * FROM StudentEnrollments
--      WHERE student_name='Ashish' AND course_id='CSE101'
--      FOR UPDATE;
--    (This locks the target row. Do NOT COMMIT yet.)
-- 3) Now keep this transaction open while you switch to Session B.

-- Session B (in a second client window while Session A's transaction is still open):
-- 1) START TRANSACTION;
-- 2) Try to UPDATE the same row:
--       UPDATE StudentEnrollments
--       SET enrollment_date = '2024-07-02'
--       WHERE student_name='Ashish' AND course_id='CSE101';
--    -> This UPDATE will be blocked (it will wait) until Session A COMMITs or ROLLBACKs.
-- 3) If you try SELECT ... FOR UPDATE in Session B it will wait too.
-- After Session A COMMIT/ROLLBACK, Session B's UPDATE will proceed (or error/complete depending).

-- Example timeline to try manually:
-- Session A:
--   START TRANSACTION;
--   SELECT * FROM StudentEnrollments WHERE student_name='Ashish' AND course_id='CSE101' FOR UPDATE;
--   -- (keep transaction open)
-- Session B:
--   START TRANSACTION;
--   UPDATE StudentEnrollments SET enrollment_date='2024-07-02'
--     WHERE student_name='Ashish' AND course_id='CSE101';
--   -- this will block until Session A commits or rollbacks
-- Session A:
--   COMMIT;  -- releasing the lock
-- Session B:
--   -- Now the UPDATE will complete; then COMMIT in Session B.

